# Copy to Frontend/.env and adjust. Never commit .env — the repository root .gitignore excludes it.
# Only variables prefixed VITE_ are exposed to browser code; anything else stays build-time only.
# Whatever is put here is readable by anyone who opens the site, so it never holds a secret.

# Base URL of the API, and it MUST end in the /api prefix the server mounts its routes under.
# Without that suffix every call resolves to a route the server does not have and answers 404.
# Must match an entry in the server's CORS_ORIGINS-approved pairing: the browser calls this URL
# from http://localhost:5173, and the server must be allowing that exact origin back.
#
# The value below is the LOCAL one, because this file is copied to Frontend/.env for development
# and is paired with the Backend/.env.example defaults, which name the Vite dev server.
# In production this is set on Vercel instead, and there it must read exactly:
#   VITE_API_URL=https://blokta.onrender.com/api
# with no surrounding whitespace — a stray space is carried into the baked bundle.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000/api

# Browser-restricted Google Maps key, used ONLY for Places Autocomplete in the client.
# It is a DIFFERENT credential from the backend's GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY and must never be the same
# value: this one is shipped to the browser, that one is a server secret.
# Enable on this key:  Places API (New)
# Restrict it by:      HTTP referrer (your site origins), and by that one API.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=

# OAuth 2.0 Client ID for Google sign-in. The SAME value as the server's GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID:
# the browser asks Google for an ID token issued to this client, and the server verifies the token
# was issued to that same client. A public identifier rather than a secret, which is why it may be
# shipped to the browser at all. It is NOT the Maps key and must never hold that value.
#
# Leaving it unset is supported: the Continue with Google button is not rendered, and email and
# password sign-in are unaffected.
VITE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
